r a defendant\'s Sixth Amendment rights were violated when they accepted a plea based on incorrect assurances about deportation, and whether State courts must follow the same rules as Federal courts in advising defendants of their rights before accepting a guilty plea.\n  - id: 15-1293, name: Lee v. Tam, description: The Supreme Court is considering whether a federal law that prohibits the registration of trademarks deemed to disparage certain groups or symbols violates free speech rights.\n  - id: 15-606, name: Pena-Rodriguez v. Colorado, description: The case concerns whether Colorado must consider evidence of racial bias when proving a violation of the Sixth Amendment right to an impartial jury, as required by other jurisdictions.\n  - id: 14-915, name: Friedrichs v. California Teachers Assn., description: Petitioners challenge the requirement that they subsidize a union that advocates an ideological viewpoint they oppose, arguing this violates their First Amendment rights.\n  - id: 14-144, name: Walker v. Texas Div., Sons of Confederate Veterans, Inc., description: The case concerns whether the State of Texas violates the First Amendment by restricting messages on license plates to official government speech only.\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this format:\n{\n    "parameters": {\n        <param_name>: <value or null>\n    },\n    "reasoning": "<brief explanation>"\n}\n',)
